Just making sure,
@hiddenone
we can use characters made in the generator as background characters/filler/npcs right?

@hiddenone
i was just thinking would using a single plugin that fixes rm font rendering like this disqualifies you from getting rtp hero badge?
https://forums.rpgmakerweb.com/index.php?threads/opentype-pixel-font-renderer-mv-mz.171027/

Me too
@TeiRaven
me too.

These were a few that caught my attention early on. I still have others to try out.
The 2026 "I Love You!" Banner, Limited Time! Available Until by
@TheAM-Dol
Well, that's one way to showcase all the different MV and MZ characters.
Loved the 'sorry for the price increase, folks...' remarks. (As an aside, if you press <esc> while on the selection screen, you get a loading error (Failed to load: img/faces/Actor1.png)
I Love You (MV w/ some MZ assets) by
@ATT_Turan
Aww, I feel badly for Marsha.  I think you should make a sequel. I'm sure once Marsha meets Eliot, she'll understand her feelings for Harold were no more than a teenage crush.
Baron von Piledriver's Puzzle Jam! (MV) by
@Wayward
Martian
Showcases 4 classic RPG puzzles. There was no save ability which caused a bit of frustration during the trial and error maze puzzle, but I could still finish the game in less than 10 minutes, even with the necessary restarts.
Reid's Secret Date (MZ) by
@Welleran
Not being good at stealth games, I had to pass on this entry.
Beast Hunters (VX Ace) by
@Axius
Link leads to a 404 itch.io page
Kitty's Day (MZ) by
@Midona018
Cute 'fetch it' game showing off some of my favorite MZ person (non-hero) characters and a nice generated character (Kitty's Mom).
Magical Girl Priscilla: Funny Farm (MZ w/ some MV assets) by
@KV_Kingdom
Ask questions to determine whether the animal is real or a demon in disguise. My answers were hit or miss.
For the Love of the RPG Maker (MZ w/ assets from 2k, 2k3, XP, VX, Ace and MV) by
@unity
Although I think the scope of this entry definitely exceeded the recommended time frame (5 hours for me), this little game was a joy to play. I loved seeing all the different RPG Maker characters, facesets and tilesets chaotically meshed in this project. This was a definite RPG Maker lovefest.
Hope's Cure (MV) by
@StarWolff
Cut scenes were well done, as were the screen transitions. I wish there were a way for Cat to heal Marsha, Horse and itself before entering the castle as the Mage hits for more damage than the during-battle Heal can restore. I did manage to survive the battle after Marsha died and was able to see the ending. Could definitely be expanded into a full fledged game.
Rise of the Farmer (MV) by
@Reim_Harbert
Cute farming sim with a surprise ending. Thoroughly enjoyed it. There were a few flaws, the White Potion claims to heal all but it only heals one, the transfer event after the final upgrade is up a little too high so every time you go back to the farm you have to cancel out the option to travel elsewhere. Despite these, the game was extremely smooth and well done.
Romancing Reid (MZ) by
@Starmage
Kind of a cross between Twilight Zone and Stepford Wives. Gave me an uncomfortable feeling, and that's a compliment to the developer.

@Solar_Flare
Thanks for giving it a shot! ^_^  I didn't want to make it too difficult since there was the time limit, also it's easier to program easy puzzles.
@Lady_JJ
Thanks for giving my game a go! ^_^  The lack of saving was mostly because if you saved in the middle of a puzzle, then left and came back, all the events reset, so if you were in the middle of the box-pushing maze you could end up trapped.  I know there's plugins for 'event stays where it's put' but I couldn't use them for the jam.  I hoped the Reset Item would make up for not being able to save.
@hiddenone
Thanks for hosting this jam! ^_^  I look forward to seeing my new badges when I hit Post Reply.

@Solar_Flare
thanks for giving it a shot.
If the typos are words missing an apostrophe, that is already known and due to how I chose to handle generating the random dialogue. If there are other typos beyond missing apostrophes, I'd appreciate knowing where those were.
